# The starting point of Kairos's kernel config: one of the ready-made configs
# that ship with Linux, named as the kernel calls it.
#
# allnoconfig turns every optional switch off. What stays on is what Linux
# can't be built without on this architecture, plus the standard basics that
# are optional only in the kernel's "expert" mode: printing messages, users
# and groups, the lock that threads use, timers.
#
# kairos.config, next to this file, holds our switches on top of it.
allnoconfig
